-- args
format --stdin-file-path input.md --wrap 40 --verify
-- stdin
This paragraph before the template blocks is long enough to wrap at the requested column.

{{< figure src="a-long-image-name.png" caption="An overwide caption that must stay exactly as authored" >}}

The paragraph between these template blocks also has enough ordinary prose to wrap across several lines.

{{% notice title="An overwide template block title that must remain exactly as authored" %}}
This   ordinary Markdown paragraph inside the shortcode should have its spacing normalized and wrap at the requested column.

{{% notice %}}
Nested   Markdown prose also wraps normally inside the surrounding shortcode.
{{% /notice %}}

Prose   after the nested shortcode still belongs to the outer Markdown body and wraps normally.
{{% /notice %}}

{{< highlight go >}}
func main() {
    fmt.Println("This overwide string stays exactly as authored inside the raw shortcode.")
}
{{< /highlight >}}

This paragraph after the template region is long enough to wrap at the requested column.
